Strategy-Pattern:-

Allows you to change behaviour of class at runtime without modifying previous code

Instead of writing multiple if-else conditions we :
  1:Create seprate strategy classes for each behaviour
  2:Use a common interface
  3:Choose strategy dynamically

Ex: 
In a payment system, User can pay using Credit card, Upi, Debit card, etc.. 
Instead of writing if else conditions we create a common interface called PaymentStrategy and different classes for Payment options.
Context class act as a wrapper it holds refrence to strategy and delegates to work seprating client from actual implementation.
  
